{
  "schema_version": "1.6.2",
  "id": "BIT-git-lfs-2026-105803",
  "summary": "Git LFS may execute arbitrary commands via crafted Git LFS configurations",
  "details": "Git LFS is a Git extension for versioning large files. From 1.3.0 until 3.8.1, Git LFS does not correctly filter the limited set of options permitted in a repository's .lfsconfig file when option keys contain certain additional components. Crafted keys can mimic options that configure Git LFS to use a custom command to transfer objects, causing Git LFS to execute an attacker-selected command or binary while fetching objects. This issue is fixed in version 3.8.1.",
